Task: review-fixes (conductor-review of track aguigraph_20260908)

Verdict was Request changes on one High; this commit closes it and the
Medium.

High — inbound _adk reached ADK session state (acceptance criterion 7):
  agui/executor.go now wraps reqState in withoutInternalKeys before
  ensureSessionForSnapshot. Verified red first: a reqState carrying _adk
  landed in session state on new-thread creation.

  Why the track missed it: FR3's stated concern is node outputs leaking
  back as host state, and the implementation read that as an OUTBOUND
  filtering problem (strip _adk from snapshots). The criterion's second
  clause, 'absent from state written back to the ADK session', is an
  INBOUND problem on a different code path. TestNodeOutputsInInterruptSnapshot
  proved the snapshot direction and made the round trip look closed.

  This track is what made it reachable: before it, nothing sent _adk to
  clients, so nothing would echo it. The pre-existing _agui_ keys share
  the hole for the same reason and are now covered too.

Medium — emitted deltas aliased the live accumulator:
  copyNodeOutputs snapshots the map into each STATE_DELTA and each
  interrupt STATE_SNAPSHOT.

  The wire was never wrong (the SSE writer serialises on Emit), which is
  why no existing test caught it. The exposure is
  AfterEventCallback(execCtx, ev, collector.Emitted): a host holding an
  emitted event saw it grow. Reproduced with a holding sink before fixing.

Design notes:
- withoutInternalKeys returns the input map unchanged when nothing is
  internal, so the common path allocates nothing, and never mutates its
  argument since the caller owns it. Both pinned by test.
- Copy is shallow. Values are opaque node outputs the launcher does not
  interpret; a deep copy would impose a structure contract the spec
  explicitly declines (outputs are carried opaquely).

